WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.880
Enniskillen, 1987.

2
00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:05.440
Marie Wilson is killed in a bombing.

3
00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:09.720
Her father, Gordon, says he
bears the bombers no ill will.

4
00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:11.320
He prays for them.

5
00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:14.650
Christians remember that
Jesus told Peter to forgive,

6
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:18.310
not seven times, but seventy times seven.

7
00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:22.870
But if you forgive someone who hurt
you, should they still be punished?

8
00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:25.500
In this mission, you'll
unpack what forgiveness,

9
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:28.860
repentance and reconciliation really mean.

10
00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:32.100
Then you'll meet people who
forgave terrible wrongs,

11
00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:35.800
and weigh up whether some
actions can never be forgiven.

12
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.590
Your mission: find out whether forgiving
someone means they should go unpunished.
